    "lawCode": "Add §809, R & SS L",
    "lawSection": "Retirement and Social Security Law",
    "memo": " BILL NUMBER:  S5628\n\n TITLE OF BILL :\nAn act to amend the retirement and social security law, in relation to\nthe purchase of service credit\n\n\n PURPOSE :\nThis bill would allow a member of the New York State and Local\nEmployees Retirement System (NYS&LERS) retirement system who has\nrendered a minimum of five years of credited service to purchase up to\nfive years of additional service credit for a period of time during\nwhich no actual service was rendered. This type of service is commonly\nreferred to as \"air time\". The full cost of such service will be paid\nby the member and it will not be available to embers in special plans.\n\n SUMMARY OF PROVISIONS :\nAdds a new section 809 to the Retirement and Social Security Law to\nallow members in the New York State and Local Employees Retirement\nSystem to purchase up to five years of additional service credit to be\nadded to the member of years the member was actually employed by a\npublic employer. The member purchasing the credit would pay the full\nactuarial cost, as determined by the comptroller. This benefit would\nnot apply to members in plans that allow for retirement regardless of\nage with 20 or 25 years of service.\n\n EXISTING LAW :\nPresent law allows members to obtain credit for prior public service\nwith a New York public employer and for certain military service.\n\n JUSTIFICATION :\nAt least twelve other States have adopted pension policies that allow\nmembers to purchase additional pension service credit, at the members'\nexpense. Planning for retirement is a complex process, with many\nvariables that affect individual and family circumstances. This bill\nwould increase the flexibility of retirement planning by allowing\nindividuals the choice to make cash payment into the retirement fund\nin exchange for additional pension service credit.  This has the\neffect of allowing members to turn and initial cash payment into a\nlifetime retirement income stream administered by NYS&LERS. Since the\nmember would pay the full cost of this additional service credit,\nthere should be little or no cost to employers or taxpayers.\n\nThis bill would provide members with a favorable alternative to\npurchasing annuities in the private market.  The NYS&LERS would,\neffectively, be providing eight percent annual interest.\n\n LEGISLATIVE HISTORY :\n2009 Session - New legislation\n\n FISCAL IMPLICATIONS :\nIf this bill is enacted, the cost to purchase \"air time\" will depend\non the member's plan, tier, age, salary current service and the amount\nof \"air time\" that will be purchased. There could be costs to NYS&LERS\non behalf of members whose salary increases subsequent to purchasing\nthis \"service\" exceed our expectations, or for members who survive\nbeyond their life expectancy. There will also be administrative costs\nto the NYS&LERS.\n\n EFFECTIVE DATE :\nNinety days after enactment.\n",
